  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>Protective spirits flit around you in a 15-foot Emanation for the duration. If you are good or neutral, their spectral form appears angelic or fey (your choice). If you are evil, they appear fiendish.</p><p>When you cast this spell, you can designate creatures to be unaffected by it. Any other creature's Speed is halved in the Emanation, and whenever the Emanation enters a creature's space and whenever a creature enters the Emanation or ends its turn there, the creature must make a Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 3d8 Radiant damage (if you are good or neutral) or 3d8 Necrotic damage (if you are evil). On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage. A creature makes this save only once per turn.</p><p><strong>Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.</strong> The damage increases by 1d8 for each spell slot level above 3.</p><p><strong>midi-qol</strong>: Requires <strong>Aura Effects</strong> module and an <strong>active combat</strong>. The Cast activity applies the Spirit Guardians aura effect to the caster (<code>selfTargetAlways</code>). Aura Effects spreads copies to enemies within 15 feet. The <code>on</code> macro creates a dependent effect on each enemy with speed halved and <code>ActivityOverTime</code> (Emanation Save at start of turn). The macro also immediately triggers the Emanation Save when the aura copy first applies (entering the emanation). Spell scaling supported (+1d8 per slot above 3). Concentration removal ends all effects.</p>",
      "chat": "<p>Protective spirits flit around you in a 15-foot Emanation for the duration. If you are good or neutral, their spectral form appears angelic or fey (your choice). If you are evil, they appear fiendish.</p><p>When you cast this spell, you can designate creatures to be unaffected by it. Any other creature's Speed is halved in the Emanation, and whenever the Emanation enters a creature's space and whenever a creature enters the Emanation or ends its turn there, the creature must make a Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 3d8 Radiant damage (if you are good or neutral) or 3d8 Necrotic damage (if you are evil). On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage. A creature makes this save only once per turn.</p><p><strong>Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.</strong> The damage increases by 1d8 for each spell slot level above 3.</p>"
    },
